---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const breadcrumbSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    {
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: 1,
      name: 'Home',
      item: 'https://www.evstartups.com',
    },
    {
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: 2,
      name: 'Affiliate & Earnings Disclaimer',
      item: 'https://www.evstartups.com/disclaimer',
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title="Affiliate & Earnings Disclaimer | evStartups.com"
  description="Affiliate, sponsorship, and lead generation compensation disclosure for evStartups.com commercial EV software directory."
  jsonLd={breadcrumbSchema}
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class="bg-slate-50 min-h-screen pb-20">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="border-b border-slate-200/80 bg-white py-12 sm:py-16">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
        <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-medium text-slate-500 mb-4">
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-slate-900 transition">Home</a>
          <span>/</span>
          <span class="text-slate-900 font-semibold">Earnings Disclaimer</span>
        </nav>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl font-['Plus_Jakarta_Sans']">
          Affiliate & Earnings Disclaimer
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-500">
          Last Updated: October 5, 2026 &bull; Transparency in B2B Research
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Main Content Container with Centered Typography -->
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 sm:p-12 shadow-xs space-y-8 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
        
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Plus_Jakarta_Sans']">
            1. Independent B2B Research Mission
          </h2>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-slate-900">evStartups.com</strong> was founded to provide transparent, hardware-agnostic research and comparative benchmarks for commercial electric fleet operators, municipal transit authorities, school bus depots, and enterprise logistics networks.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our core mission is to empower fleet decision-makers to identify the right charge point management systems (CPMS), dynamic load balancing engines, and telematics platforms for their unique operational requirements.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-slate-100 pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Plus_Jakarta_Sans']">
            2. How We Keep Our Directory Free (Compensation Disclosure)
          </h2>
          <p>
            To keep our comprehensive database, technical guides, protocol breakdowns, and comparison matrices 100% free for commercial fleet buyers, we may receive financial compensation from software vendors.
          </p>
          <p>This compensation occurs primarily through three avenues:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-slate-800">Qualified Lead Generation:</strong> When a fleet operator submits a pricing request, demo inquiry, or request for information (RFI) through our directory, we may receive a referral fee from the software vendor when we connect them with qualified buyers.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-slate-800">Sponsored Profile Enhancements:</strong> Vendors may occasionally sponsor badge placements or featured positioning in specific directory categories. Any sponsored listing will always be clearly designated as such.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-slate-800">Affiliate Partnerships:</strong> Certain platform links or partner referrals may generate affiliate compensation when commercial software trials or subscriptions are executed.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-slate-100 pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Plus_Jakarta_Sans']">
            3. Our Strict Editorial Integrity Guarantee
          </h2>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50/50 p-5 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-emerald-950">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-emerald-900 text-sm">
              Financial Compensation Does NOT Alter Technical Evaluations
            </h3>
            <p>
              We firmly believe that B2B buyer trust is our most valuable asset. Therefore, financial compensation or commercial arrangements <strong class="underline">never</strong> influence:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-emerald-900/90 text-xs sm:text-sm pt-1">
              <li>Our technical protocol verification (e.g. OCPP 1.6J, OCPP 2.0.1, ISO 15118, OpenADR).</li>
              <li>Documented hardware compatibility and telematics integrations.</li>
              <li>Our objective side-by-side software capability matrices.</li>
              <li>The identified "Considerations" or technical trade-offs listed on vendor profiles.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">
            We do not accept payment to remove legitimate technical limitations, fabricate hardware compatibility, or write favorable reviews for substandard charging platforms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-slate-100 pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Plus_Jakarta_Sans']">
            4. Fleet Operator Due Diligence
          </h2>
          <p>
            While we conduct extensive research into API architectures, local edge resilience, and power management capabilities, every commercial fleet has unique electrical constraints, vehicle duty cycles, and utility rate structures.
          </p>
          <p>
            We strongly recommend that fleet operators run pilot deployments, request test API credentials, and review vendor SLA agreements directly prior to enterprise contracting.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-slate-100 pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Plus_Jakarta_Sans']">
            5. Questions Regarding This Disclaimer
          </h2>
          <p>
            If you have any questions regarding our monetization policies, affiliate relationships, or editorial guidelines, please contact us directly at <a href="mailto:editorial@evstartups.com" class="text-emerald-600 hover:underline">editorial@evstartups.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
